WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.401
<v Narrator>Rain fell through the colossal leaves in heavy, rhythmic sheets, filling the petrified canopy with a sound like distant drumming. Fifty feet below, the forest floor was lost in twilight shadow.

2
00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:34.038
<v Narrator>High in the woven limbs of four ancient petrified giants, the Canopy Raft strained against its high-tension bungees. Ignatious leaned over the wooden gunwale, blowing a plume of grey ash through his nostrils. Faint orange embers danced along the cuffs of his heavy leather coat, fighting off the damp chill.

3
00:00:34.038 --> 00:00:34.926
<v Ignatious>"Well,"

4
00:00:34.926 --> 00:00:39.367
<v Narrator> Ignatious grunted, adjusting the warhammer strapped across his back. 

5
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:41.378
<v Ignatious>"The landing went better than I thought."

6
00:00:41.378 --> 00:00:51.853
<v Narrator>Beside him, Loami unbolted the central winch casing. He wiped grease and rainwater from his brow with the back of a calloused hand, adjusting his damp woolen flat cap.

7
00:00:51.853 --> 00:00:54.831
<v Loami>"Gotta say I'm shocked we made it up here at all,"

8
00:00:54.831 --> 00:00:59.402
<v Narrator> Loami said, his broad shoulders tensing as he checked the rig's balance. 

9
00:00:59.402 --> 00:01:03.843
<v Loami>"We look a little like a ragtag crew, but here we are. Safe as we're gonna get."

10
00:01:03.843 --> 00:01:19.360
<v Narrator>A low, resonant thud vibrated through the petrified wood beneath their boots. Miles away, through gaps in the foliage, a jagged pillar of violet lightning hammered the central Mon. The air tasted sharply of copper and ozone.

11
00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.554
<v Narrator>Ignatious squinted toward the flash. 

12
00:01:21.554 --> 00:01:28.921
<v Ignatious>"What's the purpose of all this? Is the Academy testing our adventurism, or is there a reason the sky keeps tryin' to melt the obelisk?"

13
00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:40.232
<v Narrator>Loami's expression darkened. Before entering the Academy, he had spent years servicing power conduits in Harmony, learning the temperamental pulse of Aether technology.

14
00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:41.878
<v Loami>"They've lost control,"

15
00:01:41.878 --> 00:01:46.031
<v Narrator> Loami murmured, inspecting the hum of their craft's instruments. 

16
00:01:46.031 --> 00:01:59.327
<v Loami>"The nodes broadcast a high-frequency pulse to keep canopy beasts at bay. But whatever hit the bay short-circuited the main line. The shields are down. Recovery time... eight increments, minimum."

17
00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:01.156
<v Narrator>He looked back at the party. 

18
00:02:01.156 --> 00:02:10.194
<v Loami>"We've got three clocks tickin' against us now: how long we can survive out here, when the storm surge hits, and whether this raft holds together."

19
00:02:10.194 --> 00:02:16.255
<v Narrator>Ignatious ran a gloved hand along a thick, fibrous vine clinging to the petrified trunk. 

20
00:02:16.255 --> 00:02:20.460
<v Ignatious>"Can I grab some of these vines for extra ropage? You can always use more rope."

21
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.923
<v Loami>"Hop off if you want,"

22
00:02:21.923 --> 00:02:24.588
<v Narrator> Loami said, scanning the dark canopy. 

23
00:02:24.588 --> 00:02:25.946
<v Loami>"I'm gonna scout."

24
00:02:25.946 --> 00:02:38.642
<v Narrator>Ignatious swung his boot over the rail, stepping onto a wide, moss-slick bough. But as his weight shifted, the dark foliage rustled unnaturally. He froze, clutching the vine.

25
00:02:38.642 --> 00:02:39.399
<v Ignatious>"No, no,"

26
00:02:39.399 --> 00:02:42.429
<v Narrator> Ignatious muttered, his eyes darting through the leaves. 

27
00:02:42.429 --> 00:02:53.035
<v Ignatious>"There's always somethin' hidin' out there waitin' to snap at you when you get close. All right, guys... I'm grabbin' some vines, but keep your eyes open. You nevah know when you'll need more rope."

28
00:02:53.035 --> 00:03:13.724
<v Narrator>Loami crouched low on the bough, narrowing his dark eyes. His low-light vision pierced the rain-dappled twilight. Beneath the creeping vines, sleek, four-legged silhouettes prowled across the petrified bark—lean, cat-like predators perfectly camouflaged against the dark timber.

29
00:03:13.724 --> 00:03:14.534
<v Loami>"Hey!"

30
00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:17.251
<v Narrator> Loami hissed, dropping his center of gravity. 

31
00:03:17.251 --> 00:03:21.691
<v Loami>"We've got feline creatures out on the branches! Natty, hurry back!"

32
00:03:21.691 --> 00:03:35.536
<v Narrator>Britt and Aggie scrambled up beside him, peering into the shadows. The creatures were built somewhere between a coyote and a mountain cat—territorial predators native to the upper canopy, known as Meowders.

33
00:03:35.536 --> 00:03:37.234
<v Ignatious>"A coyobi? Interesting,"

34
00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:39.063
<v Narrator> Ignatious mused.

35
00:03:39.063 --> 00:03:44.000
<v Narrator>Britt drew her hunting knife, her green skin shimmering faintly in the dim light. 

36
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.937
<v Britt>"Oh yeah, we know those! They're in our forest back home—Meowders!"

37
00:03:48.937 --> 00:03:50.060
<v Ignatious>"Seen what?"

38
00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.411
<v Narrator> Ignatious asked, blinking. 

39
00:03:52.411 --> 00:03:53.691
<v Ignatious>"What did you see?"

40
00:03:53.691 --> 00:04:04.297
<v Narrator>A sudden flurry of scurrying claws echoed across the bark. Dozens of glowing orange eyes ignited in the dark leaves surrounding the party.

41
00:04:04.297 --> 00:04:18.795
<v Narrator>At the rear of the raft, Iggy sat curled in a tight, shivering ball inside his heavy wool trench coat. His round copper goggles were slick with rain, his small clay-and-soil body rocking back and forth in sheer terror.

42
00:04:18.795 --> 00:04:20.754
<v Iggy>"The treeth have eyeth!"

43
00:04:20.754 --> 00:04:22.766
<v Narrator> Iggy whimpered, clutching his head. 

44
00:04:22.766 --> 00:04:24.229
<v Iggy>"The treeth have eyeth!"

45
00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:25.927
<v Aggie>"Those aren't trees, Iggy!"

46
00:04:25.927 --> 00:04:27.285
<v Narrator> Aggie called back. 

47
00:04:27.285 --> 00:04:29.531
<v Aggie>"They're basically just mean cats!"

48
00:04:29.531 --> 00:04:31.464
<v Narrator>Britt didn't hesitate. 

49
00:04:31.464 --> 00:04:33.424
<v Ignatious>"Natty—move over, I've got a plan!"

50
00:04:33.424 --> 00:04:35.853
<v Narrator> she shouted, vaulting past Ignatious.

51
00:04:35.853 --> 00:04:52.780
<v Narrator>She raised her hands and unleashed *Hypnotic Shimmer*. A brilliant cascade of pulsing chromatic light erupted across the bough. The radiant illusion dazzled the pack of Meowders, leaving them pawing blindly at the glowing air.

52
00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.191
<v Ignatious>"Are they dazed?!"

53
00:04:54.191 --> 00:04:55.915
<v Narrator> Ignatious called out.

54
00:04:55.915 --> 00:04:57.430
<v Britt>"They're stunned!"

55
00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.076
<v Narrator> Britt shouted back. 

56
00:04:59.076 --> 00:05:00.957
<v Britt>"Move while they're dazed!"

57
00:05:00.957 --> 00:05:03.673
<v Loami>"Do we try to move the raft or lower a branch?"

58
00:05:03.673 --> 00:05:06.469
<v Narrator> Loami asked, eyeing their position.

59
00:05:06.469 --> 00:05:08.402
<v Ignatious>"With lightning and thunder like this?"

60
00:05:08.402 --> 00:05:10.047
<v Narrator> Ignatious countered. 

61
00:05:10.047 --> 00:05:13.678
<v Ignatious>"Can we get away, or are these things gonna pursue us with bloodlust?"

62
00:05:13.678 --> 00:05:15.037
<v Aggie>"They're territorial,"

63
00:05:15.037 --> 00:05:16.212
<v Narrator> Aggie warned. 

64
00:05:16.212 --> 00:05:17.989
<v Aggie>"They won't back off easily."

65
00:05:17.989 --> 00:05:19.765
<v Ignatious>"I'm gonna try somethin' else,"

66
00:05:19.765 --> 00:05:21.306
<v Narrator> Ignatious said. 

67
00:05:21.306 --> 00:05:26.609
<v Ignatious>"Just brandishin' the flames a bit! Let's see how these cats like my dreadful visage!"

68
00:05:26.609 --> 00:05:36.065
<v Narrator> Fanning the inner furnace of his chest, he activated *Dread Visage*. A terrifying, roaring face of orange fire erupted over his features.

69
00:05:36.065 --> 00:05:39.696
<v Narrator>Loami grinned, stepping beside him with his spanner raised. 

70
00:05:39.696 --> 00:05:41.943
<v Loami>"All right, you little cats! Bring it on!"

71
00:05:41.943 --> 00:05:58.217
<v Narrator>The explosion of fire shattered the nerve of several Meowders. Screeching in terror, two of the creatures scrambled back into the foliage. But the alpha snarled, lunging forward with reckless fury, claws raking across Loami's shoulder pauldron.

72
00:05:58.217 --> 00:06:00.986
<v Loami>"Psh, these little cats can only do minor damage!"

73
00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:04.356
<v Narrator> Loami grunted, bracing as his armor absorbed the strike.

74
00:06:04.356 --> 00:06:07.856
<v Narrator>Rain drummed against the giant leaves in a steady rhythm.

75
00:06:07.856 --> 00:06:13.995
<v Narrator>Britt stepped to the edge of the limb, running her green-skinned hand along the petrified grain. 

76
00:06:13.995 --> 00:06:15.771
<v Aggie>"This forest feels wrong,"

77
00:06:15.771 --> 00:06:17.704
<v Narrator> she murmured to Aggie. 

78
00:06:17.704 --> 00:06:28.362
<v Aggie>"Fifty feet up, dead quiet... like a set built to imitate real life. And when I touch the bark, there's no hum. The Mizizi network is dead here."

79
00:06:28.362 --> 00:06:39.073
<v Narrator>Ahead on the bough, the remaining Meowders darted around Loami's boots. Loami swung a devastating right hook, but the cat twisted beneath his fist with improbable speed.

80
00:06:39.073 --> 00:06:41.215
<v Loami>"Dammit! These skimpers are quick!"

81
00:06:41.215 --> 00:06:44.402
<v Narrator> Loami spat as his fist whistled through empty air.

82
00:06:44.402 --> 00:06:45.760
<v Ignatious>"I'll help speed you up!"

83
00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:52.839
<v Narrator> Ignatious roared. Channeling his hearthfire, he pulsed a wave of invigorating energy into Loami's spirit. 

84
00:06:52.839 --> 00:06:54.198
<v Loami>"Try again!"

85
00:06:54.198 --> 00:06:58.429
<v Narrator>Loami lunged again, but the tree-cats were too nimble, nipping at his collar.

86
00:06:58.429 --> 00:07:00.362
<v Narrator>Britt's eyes brightened. 

87
00:07:00.362 --> 00:07:06.841
<v Britt>"Would it be possible to grab one of these vines and tie a lazizi? It's a traditional Mizizi hunting method!"

88
00:07:06.841 --> 00:07:11.882
<v Narrator>Ignatious turned to her in confusion, his hands still smoldering. 

89
00:07:11.882 --> 00:07:16.402
<v Ignatious>"I have no idea what a 'Lazizi' is! But if you call it out, I'll shape it!"

90
00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:18.282
<v Aggie>"I think you'd call it a lasso!"

91
00:07:18.282 --> 00:07:20.712
<v Narrator> Aggie called out, translating for Britt.

92
00:07:20.712 --> 00:07:36.882
<v Narrator>Nodding, Ignatious seized a thick length of raw vine, channeling *Shaped Material*. Flames licked along the fibers, instant-curing the wood into a supple, perfectly balanced hunting loop. He tossed it to Britt. 

93
00:07:36.882 --> 00:07:39.233
<v Britt>"There! A flawless Lazizi rope!"

94
00:07:39.233 --> 00:07:41.349
<v Narrator>Loami stared in awe. 

95
00:07:41.349 --> 00:07:44.327
<v Loami>"Holy shit, Natty, you're really good at that!"

96
00:07:44.327 --> 00:07:52.137
<v Narrator> He drew upon *Soldier's Bond*, bolstering both himself and Ignatious as they stared down the agile felines.

97
00:07:52.137 --> 00:08:05.146
<v Narrator>Britt slapped a wide-brimmed cowboy hat onto her head. Channeling her *Hunter* training, she whirled the flame-forged vine above her head while Ignatious fortified her throw with a surge of prayer dice.

98
00:08:05.146 --> 00:08:06.922
<v Britt>"Cazito! I got ya now!"

99
00:08:06.922 --> 00:08:10.136
<v Narrator> Britt yelled as the loop sailed through the tempest wind. 

100
00:08:10.136 --> 00:08:11.416
<v Britt>"Come here, you!"

101
00:08:11.416 --> 00:08:19.148
<v Narrator>The loop snapped tight around their necks, bundling the three Meowders together like a litter of house cats picked up by the scruff.

102
00:08:19.148 --> 00:08:27.951
<v Narrator>Britt planted her boots, spun the entire cluster around her head in a roaring arc, and pitched them off the bough into the fifty-foot abyss below.

103
00:08:27.951 --> 00:08:29.048
<v Britt>"LAZIZI!"

104
00:08:29.048 --> 00:08:30.589
<v Narrator> she screamed.

105
00:08:30.589 --> 00:08:34.508
<v Narrator>Loami howled with laughter, clapping Ignatious on the shoulder. 

106
00:08:34.508 --> 00:08:36.624
<v Ignatious>"What a Kazizi-boy! Bye, gazitos!"

107
00:08:36.624 --> 00:08:39.889
<v Narrator>Ignatious blinked, wiping soot from his brow. 

108
00:08:39.889 --> 00:08:42.371
<v Ignatious>"I don't know what any of these words mean!"

109
00:08:42.371 --> 00:08:43.886
<v Loami>"It's Spanish!"

110
00:08:43.886 --> 00:08:45.584
<v Narrator> Loami yelled back. 

111
00:08:45.584 --> 00:08:46.864
<v Loami>"A gazito!"

112
00:08:46.864 --> 00:08:48.327
<v Ignatious>"Yeah, that doesn't help,"

113
00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:53.029
<v Narrator> Ignatious replied, scratching his head as they turned back toward the raft.

114
00:08:53.029 --> 00:08:58.749
<v Narrator>As the Meowders vanished into the understory, a shrill screech echoed from above.

115
00:08:58.749 --> 00:09:05.881
<v Narrator>A massive shadow cut through the driving rain. A high-pitched, furious voice echoed through the upper canopy:

116
00:09:05.881 --> 00:09:10.870
<v Pip>"NO! MY BISCUIT! NOT THESE! THESE ARE MINE, YOU FLAPPING FUZZBALL!"

117
00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.699
<v Narrator> Pip screamed from above.

118
00:09:12.699 --> 00:09:14.527
<v Narrator>Loami's head snapped upward. 

119
00:09:14.527 --> 00:09:15.833
<v Loami>"Is that Pip?!"

120
00:09:15.833 --> 00:09:26.309
<v Narrator>High above, tiny halfling legs were kicking frantically in mid-air. Pip was trapped in the talons of a monstrous Storm Raptor flying across the high branches.

121
00:09:26.309 --> 00:09:29.522
<v Pip>"LET ME GO, YOU STUPID BIRD! DON'T TOUCH MY BISCUITS!"

122
00:09:29.522 --> 00:09:30.697
<v Narrator> Pip screamed.

123
00:09:30.697 --> 00:09:33.910
<v Loami>"I'm climbin' to the top of the canopy to get in range!"

124
00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.470
<v Narrator> Loami shouted, scrambling up the slick bark.

125
00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:43.314
<v Narrator>The instant Aggie's boots touched the upper branch, the entire forest erupted in a rush of telepathic whispers: *

126
00:09:43.314 --> 00:09:45.326
<v Aggie>"Aggie, Aggie, Aggie, Aggie!"

127
00:09:45.326 --> 00:09:45.535
<v Narrator>*

128
00:09:45.535 --> 00:10:11.056
<v Narrator>Aggie closed her eyes, listening as the ancient roots poured impressions into her mind. She turned to the squad, translating the rustling plant-whispers. A 'little tree'—Bramble—had been using *Speak to Plants* to send signals through the network. He apologized through the arbol telephone network, explaining he had been seeding false signals to confuse rival salvagers.

129
00:10:11.056 --> 00:10:12.336
<v Ignatious>"That son of a bitch!"

130
00:10:12.336 --> 00:10:14.269
<v Narrator> Ignatious swore fondly.

131
00:10:14.269 --> 00:10:28.036
<v Narrator>Aggie's eyes widened as the vision clarified. Bramble had realized Squad 907 was in the forest and was trying to reach them because Pip had run out alone before the storm to fetch emergency breakfast pastries!

132
00:10:28.036 --> 00:10:31.719
<v Narrator>Above them, the Storm Raptor carrying Pip circled closer.

133
00:10:31.719 --> 00:10:36.996
<v Narrator>On the raft deck, hearing Pip's screams shattered Iggy's paralysis instantly. 

134
00:10:36.996 --> 00:10:38.824
<v Iggy>"I have to help her!"

135
00:10:38.824 --> 00:10:42.325
<v Narrator> he shouted, surging to his feet and raising his wooden staff. 

136
00:10:42.325 --> 00:10:43.971
<v Iggy>"Eth-ereal Wall!"

137
00:10:43.971 --> 00:10:55.543
<v Narrator>A fifty-foot barrier of shimmering translucent force erupted in mid-air. The Storm Raptor screeched, slamming full-force into the wall and beating its wings weakly against the barrier.

138
00:10:55.543 --> 00:11:00.584
<v Pip>"Stupid bird! Watch where you're flyin'! You're gonna make me drop my biscuits!"

139
00:11:00.584 --> 00:11:05.443
<v Narrator> Pip yelled, clutching her canvas pouch as golden crumbs rained down.

140
00:11:05.443 --> 00:11:08.996
<v Narrator>Ignatious squinted into the rain, muttering to himself, 

141
00:11:08.996 --> 00:11:12.209
<v Ignatious>"Hmm... are English biscuits or nice southern biscuits?!"

142
00:11:12.209 --> 00:11:20.908
<v Narrator>Hesitating only a second as the bird hung stalled against the barrier, Ignatious raised his hand and fired a bolt of pure flame at the Raptor. 

143
00:11:20.908 --> 00:11:27.282
<v Ignatious>"This bird glows! It's vulnerable! I saved you! You're welcome! I love it when a plan comes together!"

144
00:11:27.282 --> 00:11:45.933
<v Narrator>The impact forced the hawk's talons open, dropping Pip into open air. But as she fell, three bioluminescent shadows bounded out of the foliage—Mwaza-Chui, apex canopy jaguars lured by the rich scent of warm butter and caramelized bacon.

145
00:11:45.933 --> 00:11:48.049
<v Narrator>Loami sprinted toward the drop zone. 

146
00:11:48.049 --> 00:11:52.072
<v Loami>"Hey! You want a piece of this?! Come and get a little piece of this!"

147
00:11:52.072 --> 00:12:00.640
<v Narrator>Two jaguars darted past him, while the third leapt and caught Pip by her ponytail in its massive jaws, dangling her over the edge!

148
00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.853
<v Ignatious>"How many god's damn cats are in this gods damn forest!"

149
00:12:03.853 --> 00:12:05.551
<v Narrator> Ignatious bellowed.

150
00:12:05.551 --> 00:12:19.187
<v Narrator>The jaguar opened its jaws and unleashed *Frequency Overload*—a roaring cone of static ember energy that rocked Loami and Iggy, suppressing their spellcasting under a wave of psychic shock.

151
00:12:19.187 --> 00:12:23.941
<v Narrator>Pip dangled over the abyss, smacking the predator's snout with her food bag. 

152
00:12:23.941 --> 00:12:26.057
<v Pip>"These are my biscuits! Stop it!"

153
00:12:26.057 --> 00:12:36.663
<v Narrator>Suddenly, the tempest peaked. The colossal trees bent in half under a howling hurricane gale that battered the canopy with sleet and hail.

154
00:12:36.663 --> 00:12:55.915
<v Narrator>Reacting instantly, Ignatious used *Shaped Material* to form a wooden shield against the sleet. Aggie ran beneath the limb using *Wall Walk*, placed her palm against the bark, and channeled *Wild Fortress*, growing a complete Tree Igloo of living root-vines around Pip and Loami.

155
00:12:55.915 --> 00:12:59.311
<v Aggie>"Loami, get into the shell! I can protect you from the storm!"

156
00:12:59.311 --> 00:13:01.192
<v Narrator> Aggie shouted through the wind.

157
00:13:01.192 --> 00:13:09.603
<v Narrator>Loami dived over Pip, rolling them both into the wooden dome like a player recovering a fumble, just as the root-vines sealed tight.

158
00:13:09.603 --> 00:13:12.633
<v Narrator>Inside the quiet Tree Igloo, Pip gasped, 

159
00:13:12.633 --> 00:13:14.880
<v Pip>"I just wanted to get some snacks, man!"

160
00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:18.485
<v Loami>"I know you did, Pip! That does sound about right,"

161
00:13:18.485 --> 00:13:21.254
<v Narrator> Loami replied, catching his breath.

162
00:13:21.254 --> 00:13:25.068
<v Narrator>Leaning back against the root wall, Loami looked over at Pip. 

163
00:13:25.068 --> 00:13:34.602
<v Pip>"So here's my theory: I think they created this challenge for first-years, and somethin' went terribly wrong and short-circuited. Are you familiar with the Day of Sparks?"

164
00:13:34.602 --> 00:13:36.327
<v Pip>"It's the Night of Sparks!"

165
00:13:36.327 --> 00:13:40.846
<v Narrator> Pip corrected chidingly, opening her bag of snacks to inspect the damage. 

166
00:13:40.846 --> 00:13:43.615
<v Pip>"Did you not listen to anythin' they taught us in school?!"

167
00:13:43.615 --> 00:13:44.477
<v Loami>"Uh, no,"

168
00:13:44.477 --> 00:13:45.940
<v Narrator> Loami admitted. 

169
00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:54.743
<v Loami>"But the Night of Sparks—that was about havin' too much power. It was too little power here! The shields went down, and all these beasts started stormin' the ring!"

170
00:13:54.743 --> 00:14:04.513
<v Narrator>Outside, through the gale, stadium speakers crackled across the sky: *Just hold on... halfway... shield crack up... hold on!*

171
00:14:04.513 --> 00:14:16.973
<v Narrator>In the bay below, a giant iron steamship—the *Deep-Hull*—rose through the waves, its heavy steam cannons firing pulse rounds to push back beasts attacking the center spire.

172
00:14:16.973 --> 00:14:27.109
<v Narrator>Outside the Igloo, as the storm wall passed, Ignatious looked at his boots, then up into the sky, before slapping his own forehead in sudden realization.

173
00:14:27.109 --> 00:14:28.415
<v Ignatious>"Wait a minute,"

174
00:14:28.415 --> 00:14:30.296
<v Narrator> Ignatious realized aloud. 

175
00:14:30.296 --> 00:14:31.654
<v Ignatious>"I can fucking fly!"

176
00:14:31.654 --> 00:14:40.718
<v Narrator>Ignatious ignited his ember wings, soaring up with his warhammer to strike the glowing Storm Raptor, sending it crashing into the underbrush.

177
00:14:40.718 --> 00:14:54.354
<v Narrator>Meanwhile, the pack of Mwaza-Chui slammed against the exterior of the Tree Igloo, their claws punching at the timber. Within, Pip and Loami sat in comfort, scarfing down a biscuit each.

178
00:14:54.354 --> 00:14:57.724
<v Loami>"This biscuit is great, I can feel the stress drainin' away!"

179
00:14:57.724 --> 00:14:59.918
<v Narrator> Loami exclaimed between bites.

180
00:14:59.918 --> 00:15:01.512
<v Pip>"Yeah, I'm nevah stressed!"

181
00:15:01.512 --> 00:15:04.464
<v Narrator> Pip replied through a mouthful of buttery flakes.

182
00:15:04.464 --> 00:15:09.453
<v Narrator>Suddenly, a jaguar snout breached the dome, roaring into the igloo.

183
00:15:09.453 --> 00:15:10.916
<v Loami>"Pip, watch out!"

184
00:15:10.916 --> 00:15:14.599
<v Narrator> Loami yelled, jumping to cover her. But Pip simply dodged.

185
00:15:14.599 --> 00:15:15.592
<v Pip>"Bad cat!"

186
00:15:15.592 --> 00:15:24.709
<v Narrator> Pip scolded, popping up and bopping the jaguar on the nose with her bag of food. The jaguar froze, scrunching its nose in shock.

187
00:15:24.709 --> 00:15:31.082
<v Narrator>Outside, Britt and Iggy gathered a massive pile of phosphorescent mushrooms along the trunk. 

188
00:15:31.082 --> 00:15:37.273
<v Britt>"In Mizizi lore, jaguars are super attracted to bioluminescent light! I have a plan,"

189
00:15:37.273 --> 00:15:41.976
<v Narrator> Britt said, collecting spores while Iggy stacked them on the raft deck.

190
00:15:41.976 --> 00:15:57.832
<v Narrator>Aggie channeled *Conjure Swarm*, sending a trail of glowing fireflies toward the bait. The scent and brilliant glow caught the jaguars' nostrils. Turning away from the Igloo, the pack bounded onto the raft deck to gorge on the fungi.

191
00:15:57.832 --> 00:15:59.660
<v Narrator>Pip started to yell, 

192
00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:01.254
<v Aggie>"Hey, you big furbag—!"

193
00:16:01.254 --> 00:16:03.030
<v Narrator> before Aggie shushed her.

194
00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:11.651
<v Narrator>As the cats gorged, Loami stalked behind them. Waiting until all three were on the deck, Loami heaved his shoulder against the timber. 

195
00:16:11.651 --> 00:16:13.767
<v Loami>"Now! Push together and cut the bungees!"

196
00:16:13.767 --> 00:16:15.229
<v Narrator> Loami yelled.

197
00:16:15.229 --> 00:16:23.327
<v Narrator>Britt slashed the high-tension bungees. Loami and Iggy heaved with all their strength, tipping the Canopy Raft off the branch.

198
00:16:23.327 --> 00:16:34.064
<v Narrator>The raft pitched over, sending the entire pack of Mwaza-Chui plummeting fifty feet into the dark abyss below with echoing roars and a heavy crash.

199
00:16:34.064 --> 00:16:37.799
<v Narrator>Across the branch, a second Storm Raptor lunged at Iggy.

200
00:16:37.799 --> 00:16:39.497
<v Loami>"Natty, bring it this way!"

201
00:16:39.497 --> 00:16:41.613
<v Narrator> Loami shouted across the canopy.

202
00:16:41.613 --> 00:16:58.802
<v Narrator>Ignatious dodged a talon strike and streaked across the bough. As the Raptor dived, Loami stepped in, shielding Ignatious with a well-timed punch that countered the talons. Frustrated and outnumbered, the Raptor screeched and fled into the storm.

203
00:16:58.802 --> 00:17:00.212
<v Ignatious>"Oh my gods, thank you!"

204
00:17:00.212 --> 00:17:02.145
<v Narrator> Ignatious gasped.

205
00:17:02.145 --> 00:17:06.064
<v Loami>"I figured a little one-on-one with one of those things wasn't a fair fight,"

206
00:17:06.064 --> 00:17:07.422
<v Narrator> Loami said.

207
00:17:07.422 --> 00:17:10.609
<v Ignatious>"The one-on-one was fine. The two-on-one aftahward was not!"

208
00:17:10.609 --> 00:17:12.333
<v Narrator> Ignatious laughed.

209
00:17:12.333 --> 00:17:19.647
<v Narrator>The wind died down to a light, cool sprinkle. Sitting across the bough was Pip, gnawing on her jerky.

210
00:17:19.647 --> 00:17:31.455
<v Narrator>Behind her sat Mwaza-Kasa—the sacred Spirit Tortoise of the Mizizi clan, its bark-like shell looming over Pip, its glassy eyes flicking between Aggie and Britt.

211
00:17:31.455 --> 00:17:33.388
<v Ignatious>"Is that... a family membah of yours?"

212
00:17:33.388 --> 00:17:35.086
<v Narrator> Ignatious whispered.

213
00:17:35.086 --> 00:17:38.064
<v Loami>"It's just sittin' there loomin'... menacingly,"

214
00:17:38.064 --> 00:17:39.474
<v Narrator> Loami noted.

215
00:17:39.474 --> 00:17:44.594
<v Narrator>Britt gestured frantically for Pip to back away, but Pip reached into her bag.

216
00:17:44.594 --> 00:17:45.953
<v Pip>"I found a big turtle!"

217
00:17:45.953 --> 00:17:50.602
<v Narrator> Pip announced, holding out a biscuit. The tortoise snapped it down in one bite. 

218
00:17:50.602 --> 00:17:52.065
<v Pip>"See, it's my friend!"

219
00:17:52.065 --> 00:17:54.678
<v Narrator> Pip exulted, scratching under its chin.

220
00:17:54.678 --> 00:17:55.670
<v Britt>"Don't—!"

221
00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.264
<v Narrator> Britt gasped.

222
00:17:57.264 --> 00:18:10.064
<v Narrator>The moment Pip touched its chin, a deep *BOOM* echoed as the tortoise collapsed, its eyes glowing ember-red. Pip's eyes rolled back, and she collapsed down the branch.

223
00:18:10.064 --> 00:18:19.598
<v Narrator>Aggie sprinted forward, catching Pip before she slipped off the edge. Pip was already convulsing in her arms—entering the mycelium network alone.

224
00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:25.789
<v Britt>"You can nevah go through the network alone, or you get pulled in and nevah come out! How do we anchor her?!"

225
00:18:25.789 --> 00:18:27.200
<v Narrator> Britt cried.

226
00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:34.096
<v Aggie>"Touching Mwaza-Kasa is taboo to the Mizizi, but in absence of the trees, it acts as a physical anchor!"

227
00:18:34.096 --> 00:18:35.455
<v Narrator> Aggie realized. 

228
00:18:35.455 --> 00:18:38.668
<v Aggie>"We have to touch the living sacred tortoise to save Pip!"

229
00:18:38.668 --> 00:18:40.496
<v Narrator>Britt grabbed Aggie's hand. 

230
00:18:40.496 --> 00:18:42.456
<v Aggie>"Three... two... one!"

231
00:18:42.456 --> 00:18:52.774
<v Narrator>Pip immediately calmed into a peaceful sleep in Aggie's arms. Simultaneously, Aggie and Britt slumped forward against the shell, entering the deep network.

232
00:18:52.774 --> 00:18:54.472
<v Narrator>Ignatious blinked. 

233
00:18:54.472 --> 00:19:04.555
<v Ignatious>"Hey, Loami! What's with the weird glowin' turtle?! Everyone who touches that turtle falls asleep! Am I the crazy one here?! We should NOT touch that turtle!"

234
00:19:04.555 --> 00:19:07.115
<v Loami>"I think it might be a little too late for that,"

235
00:19:07.115 --> 00:19:11.869
<v Narrator> Loami replied sardonically, stepping forward with his hand outstretched.

236
00:19:11.869 --> 00:19:21.117
<v Narrator>Touching Mwaza-Kasa plunged Aggie and Britt into the deep network. They found Pip easily, lost in a vast, silent forest.

237
00:19:21.117 --> 00:19:25.584
<v Narrator>As they reached her side, the network unlocked a forgotten memory:

238
00:19:25.584 --> 00:19:52.124
<v Narrator>Young child versions of Aggie and Britt were laughing as they ran through a sunlit sacred grove—a memory wiped from their minds years ago. In the memory, the children sat on a mossy root to rest. But as adult Aggie and Britt watched, they saw the root open its eyes. It was a Spirit Tortoise. The moment the children touched it, they passed out, and the vision shattered.

239
00:19:52.124 --> 00:20:03.984
<v Narrator>Memories played across the bark like moving shadows: they remembered lost clan members who had vanished years ago after dying of the green shell rot currently on Britt's arm.

240
00:20:03.984 --> 00:20:08.686
<v Narrator>In their adult bodies, Britt and Aggie grabbed Pip's arms and pulled.

241
00:20:08.686 --> 00:20:17.071
<v Narrator>Loami was inches from touching the shell when Britt, Aggie, and Pip's eyes snapped open back on the high branch, gasping for breath!

242
00:20:17.071 --> 00:20:19.030
<v Loami>"Hey! Whoa! What happened?!"

243
00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:20.493
<v Narrator> Loami asked.

244
00:20:20.493 --> 00:20:21.669
<v Aggie>"You saw that?!"

245
00:20:21.669 --> 00:20:24.046
<v Narrator> Aggie gasped, staring at Britt.

246
00:20:24.046 --> 00:20:26.188
<v Britt>"Yeah... I definitely saw that,"

247
00:20:26.188 --> 00:20:27.886
<v Narrator> Britt said, shaken. 

248
00:20:27.886 --> 00:20:30.681
<v Britt>"We were kids... in the sacred grove..."

249
00:20:30.681 --> 00:20:31.961
<v Ignatious>"What?! Saw what?!"

250
00:20:31.961 --> 00:20:33.737
<v Narrator> Ignatious asked.

251
00:20:33.737 --> 00:20:36.297
<v Pip>"WHAT THE SHIT WAS THAT, MR TURTLE!?"

252
00:20:36.297 --> 00:20:38.962
<v Narrator> Pip screamed, glaring at the tortoise.

253
00:20:38.962 --> 00:20:52.545
<v Narrator>Mwaza-Kasa stood slowly on four legs, looking sad and determined. It stomped its heavy foot twice against the bark, tucked its limbs into its shell, and rolled off the edge of the fifty-foot branch!

254
00:20:52.545 --> 00:20:53.486
<v Iggy>"OH NO!"

255
00:20:53.486 --> 00:20:54.609
<v Narrator> Iggy yelled.

256
00:20:54.609 --> 00:20:55.889
<v Narrator>*CRASH!*

257
00:20:55.889 --> 00:21:08.637
<v Narrator>The shell plunged fifty feet, smashing into the ground with a thud that created a dirt crater. Moments later, the tortoise popped out of its shell, looked up at Squad 907, and waited.

258
00:21:08.637 --> 00:21:10.570
<v Loami>"Well... that can't be right!"

259
00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:11.980
<v Narrator> Loami said.

260
00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:13.757
<v Ignatious>"I think it wants you to follow it!"

261
00:21:13.757 --> 00:21:15.350
<v Narrator> Ignatious said.

262
00:21:15.350 --> 00:21:17.884
<v Britt>"Well, I'm definitely not jumpin' off the tree!"

263
00:21:17.884 --> 00:21:19.190
<v Narrator> Britt said.

264
00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.731
<v Ignatious>"I can carry one of you down!"

265
00:21:20.731 --> 00:21:22.377
<v Narrator> Ignatious offered.

266
00:21:22.377 --> 00:21:23.892
<v Narrator>Loami shrugged. 

267
00:21:23.892 --> 00:21:28.960
<v Loami>"I've fallen from furthah! Besides... I'm nevah stayin' up in these trees alone!"

268
00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:40.088
<v Narrator>Loami dived fifty feet straight down into the crater. Slamming into the dirt, he staggered to his feet and bowed deeply to Mwaza-Kasa. The sacred tortoise nodded in approval.

269
00:21:40.088 --> 00:21:44.477
<v Narrator>Britt used *Wall Walk* to carry Pip down, who grumbled, 

270
00:21:44.477 --> 00:21:45.339
<v Pip>"My headdd."

271
00:21:45.339 --> 00:21:50.198
<v Narrator> Iggy walked over and hand-fed Pip bacon biscuits as she cried tears of relief.

272
00:21:50.198 --> 00:21:59.001
<v Narrator>Mwaza-Kasa looked at Squad 907, nodded slowly, and turned to lead them on foot into the petrified forest as dawn broke.
